Windows installer: JusPrin's pictures, a Run box, no developer folders
The installer showed NSIS's generic computer on its welcome and finish
pages, a blank box at the top left of the other pages (NSIS cannot draw
the .ico CPack uses there), and "Nullsoft Install System v3.13" above the
buttons. Its finish page had no way to open the app, and it installed
stb_dxt's header and CMake export files into include\ and lib\cmake\.

- brand_logo.py draws the side picture (stacked lockup on Mist) and the
  header picture (horizontal lockup on White) as the BMPs NSIS needs.
- The line above the buttons reads "JusPrin <version>".
- The finish page has a "Run JusPrin" box. installer.nsh starts the app
  through Explorer, so it runs as the signed-in user rather than as
  administrator, where Windows would block files dragged into it.
- InstallCleanup removes the stb_dxt files and the folders left empty,
  after every other install rule, so the installer, the portable zip and
  the install folder all leave them out.

